Backport of fontforge/fontforge#5681 ("Quickfix a collision between
ttf_flags and ps_flags", commit 4a69512e, 2026-02-06) to 20251009.

The generate() flag word carries both enum ttf_flags and enum ps_flags
(see _DoSave in savefont.c, which tests ttf_native_kern, ttf_flag_ofm,
ps_flag_tfm, ps_flag_afm and ps_flag_outputfontlog on the same int), but
the two enums overlapped: ps_flag_nohints (0x40000 = 1 << 18) is also
ttf_flag_no_outlines, so font.generate(path, flags=['no-hints', ...])
wrote a font with no CFF or glyf table at all (fontforge/fontforge#5678).
ps_flag_noflex (1 << 17) likewise collided with ttf_flag_fake_map and
ps_flag_nohintsubs (1 << 16) with ttf_native_kern.

Upstream's fix drops the unused ps_flag_nohintsubs / ps_flag_restrict256
and renumbers ps_flags above the ttf_flags. 20251009 still has
ttf_flag_fake_map (removed upstream in #5736, which does not apply here),
so the layout differs from upstream's: ps_flags take bits 19 to 28, and
ps_flag_identitycidmap shares bit 17 with ttf_flag_fake_map.

Sharing that bit is safe here, but not because the two flags stay in
separate flag words: identitycidmap does reach the sfnt writer. print.c
(1545) passes it to _WritePSFont for ff_type42cid, dumppfa.c (2158) then
calls _WriteType42SFNTS, and tottf.c (6355) runs ATinit/initTables on
those flags. The two reasons it cannot be mistaken for fake_map are:

  - ttf_flag_fake_map is read only in _WriteTTFFont (tottf.c 6170 and
    6223), never in _WriteType42SFNTS or in the shared table code.
  - Its only setter is the GUI shaper (fontforgeexe/shapers/harfbuzz.cpp
    50), which this package does not build (-DENABLE_GUI=OFF).

Whoever drops this patch at the next release should check those two
facts rather than the bit numbers.

